# Check out text files with LF everywhere, including Windows.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF in the working
# tree while the index stays LF. Thirteen of the scripts/check-*.ts read source
# files and match on literal "\n", so they fail on Windows and nowhere else. CI
# runs on ubuntu-latest, so it never sees it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
